# Shared environment variables for the Next.js UI and Express API belong here.
# Copy this file to .env at the repository root.
#
# scripts/validate-env.mjs treats this file as the manifest of what has to be
# set, and `ui`, `deploy-ui`, `deploy-api`, and `e2e` all check it before doing
# any work. A variable is required in every mode by default; a marker comment
# scopes everything after it, until the next marker:
#
#   # @all               required in every mode (the default)
#   # @development-only  local work only (development and test)
#   # @non-production    everything except production (dev, test, staging)
#   # @non-development   every deployed mode (staging and production)
#   # @production-only   production deploys only
#   # @test-only         required only by `npm run e2e`
#   # @optional          documented, never required
#
# The two "non-" scopes mirror the guards the code actually uses, which is what
# makes staging expressible: @non-development matches `!IS_DEV` (a real secret
# rather than a dev literal) and @non-production matches `!IS_PROD` (a test key
# rather than the live one). Reach for them whenever staging and production
# differ — a live API key is @production-only, but its sandbox counterpart is
# @non-production, and a session secret that dev fakes is @non-development.
#
# Secrets belong here, not in a file under /home/ecarlson10/pw/. Only secrets
# genuinely shared across repos still live in pw (the MariaDB password in pw/0
# and the shared mailbox passwords), so that rotating one is a single edit rather
# than one per repo — those have no variable name and are read by path.
#
# Pick the narrowest marker that is still true. @production-only is right for a
# secret prod needs but local work does not (a live API key where dev uses a
# sandbox); marking that @all would make `npm run ui` demand it. Note that `test`
# implies development, since the e2e suite drives the local dev stack.
#
# Everything below is an inert example: the extra leading "#" keeps both the
# markers and the assignments from being parsed, so a fresh clone requires
# nothing and `npm run ui` works out of the box. Uncomment what you need.
#
#   SOME_SHARED_SECRET=
#
#   # @development-only
#   STRIPE_TEST_SECRET_KEY=
#
#   # @test-only
#   E2E_EMAIL=
#   E2E_PASSWORD=
#
#   # @optional
#   SOME_FEATURE_FLAG=
